"current_statement_sha256":"sha256:0b0fa8c5d6520a091c750085b600b40ac240a66daa1badea1a650f526b3da36b","file":"preprints/Midpoint-convexity-from-two-recursive-potentials-September-27-2026/build/sections/foundations.tex","line":65,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"3c97ad2f9bbec82a38055b9f556498d2c3ceb5801305e6c7612f7c864f4983de","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Midpoint-convexity-from-two-recursive-potentials-September-27-2026/build/sections/foundations.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:0b0fa8c5d6520a091c750085b600b40ac240a66daa1badea1a650f526b3da36b","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Midpoint-convexity-from-two-recursive-potentials-September-27-2026/build/sections/foundations.tex#L65"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{rec:main}\\label{rec:joined-root-stability}\nFor $N=N_\\Sigma$ on $X_\\Sigma$, or $N=N_J$ on $X_J$, one has\n\\begin{equation}\\label{rec:sum-modulus}\n \\widehat\\delta_N(t)\\ge t^3/128\\qquad(0<t<1).\n\\end{equation}\nFor $X_0$, a finite initial set $H$, a vector $x$ supported in $H$, and\n$z\\in F_H\\setminus\\{0\\}$, one has\n\\begin{equation}\\label{rec:equal-estimate}\n \\frac{N_0(x+z)+N_0(x-z)}2\\ge N_0(x)\n +\\frac{N_0(z)^3}{8(2N_0(x)+N_0(z))^2}.\n\\end{equation}\nEach of $X_\\Sigma,X_0,X_J$ admits no equivalent AUC norm."}
